{{/*
Who git trusts to have signed a commit locally (§6.5). It holds exactly the live
identities: no retired key is carried, because an ssh signature embeds the signer's public
key and a dropped line is reconstructible from any commit it signed (ADR 0008). Because
nothing accumulates here, no pruning rule has to exist.

Each line derives its key from the public key *file* rather than transcribing the blob a
second time — the personal one from the file in this repository, the work one from the
same 1Password field ~/.ssh/id_work.pub renders from.
*/ -}}
